.SH NAME
ixdomain \- convert weighting domain files

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/bin/ixdomain
[\ \fB\-dhwDH\fR\ ] [\ \fIfile\fR\ ...\ ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Notice:
.B ixdomain
is now obsolete. Its functionality is provided
by the more general program
.BR ixparse (1).
.PP

.B ixdomain
converts weighting domain files
between three different formats.
Weighting domains can be converted between
domain format as defined by the IXWeightingDomain
class of the Indexing Kit,
histogram format, and NEXTSTEP Release 2
word frequency table (WFTable) format.
Domain format files are preferred for use
with
.BR ixbuild (1).
.PP
Each line of a file in histogram format has the form:
.nf
.IP
.I token weight rank
.fi
.PP
Where \fItoken\fR is the token or word in the index,
\fIweight\fR is its weight (frequency) in the domain,
and \fIrank\fR is its cardinal rank in the domain
(1 == most common, 2 = second most common, and so on).
The fields of the line are separated by single spaces;
be sure to search backward from the end of a line to
find the token, as it is possible for it to
contain embedded spaces or tabs.

.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\fB\-\|\-\fR"
Lists these options.
.IP "\fB\-d\fR"
Reads domain format.
.IP "\fB\-h\fR"
Reads histogram format (default).
.IP "\fB\-w\fR"
Reads WFTable format.
.IP "\fB\-D\fR"
Writes domain format (default).
.IP "\fB\-H\fR"
Writes histogram format.

.SH SEE ALSO
ixparse(1), ixbuild(1), ixsearch(1),
Indexing Kit Documentation in \fINEXTSTEP General Reference\fR
